# .gcloudignore — files NOT uploaded to Cloud Build by `gcloud builds submit`.
#
# When this file is absent, gcloud uses `.gitignore` as the upload-exclude
# basis. That breaks deploys because `infra/terraform.tfvars` is gitignored
# (it contains secrets like db_initial_password), but Cloud Build needs it
# to apply the configured deployment (identity_provider, billing flags,
# firebase keys, monitoring, etc. — none of which the YAML passes as
# explicit -var flags).
#
# This file makes the upload rules explicit and KEEPS infra/terraform.tfvars
# included.

# --- VCS / IDE / Agent noise ---
.git/
.gitignore
.gcloudignore
.dockerignore
.github/
.vscode/
.idea/
.claude/
.gemini/
.cursorrules
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.agents/
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
GEMINI.md
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# --- Local dev environment files (MUST NOT ship to Cloud Build) ---
# scripts/deploy/deploy.py calls load_dotenv(override=True), so any .env
# file in the upload would override Cloud Build's PROJECT_ID env var.
# .env.example stays out too (harmless, but no reason to ship it).
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!infra/terraform.tfvars   # explicit allow — see note below

# --- Local dev / build / test caches (don't ship to Cloud Build) ---
.venv/
.venv*/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.uv_cache/
.mypy_cache/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
dist/
build/
**/dist/
**/build/
.angular/
**/.angular/
tests/
concepts/
.harness-runs/
docs/plans/
agents/catalog.json
.adk/
.port-slot
.worktrees/
docker-compose.override.yml
.coverage
coverage.out
coverage.html
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# --- Logs and runtime data ---
logs/
**/logs/
*.log
data/
**/data/
scratch/
scratch.py

# --- Terraform local state (state lives in GCS) ---
infra/.terraform/
infra/.terraform.lock.hcl
infra/*.tfstate
infra/*.tfstate.*
infra/errored.tfstate*
infra/*.tfplan
infra/tfplan
infra/services.auto.tfvars.json
infra/tests.disabled/
# Each module subdir gets its own .terraform/providers/ when tofu init is
# run locally — ~115 MiB per provider mirror. Cloud Build downloads fresh
# providers from the registry; don't ship the local cache.
infra/modules/**/.terraform/
infra/**/.terraform.lock.hcl

# --- Stale local binaries at repo root (Cloud Build rebuilds from src) ---
/admin
/billing
/frontend
/gateway
/tester
/stress
alloydb-auth-proxy

# NOTE: infra/terraform.tfvars IS uploaded so Cloud Build's terraform apply
# can read identity_provider, enable_billing_service, firebase_*,
# alert_email, etc. The file contains db_initial_password —
# the Cloud Build staging bucket is project-internal (IAM-controlled).
# Rotate the password via Secret Manager after first apply.
